From: atchoum31 <16476634+atchoum31@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:25:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Enable OTA on Zectrix boards with an image check

OTA was off so that an official TRMNL image could not reach a Zectrix
board. Turn it on, and pass the download through ZectrixImageCheck.
Every image built for the board contains ZECTRIX_IMAGE_ID
("TRMNL-ZECTRIX-IMAGE:<model>"). When the ID is missing, the update is
aborted before the image becomes bootable.

OTA writes only the app partition, so the settings stay on the device.
---
 docs/zectrix.md                  |  6 ++++--
 include/zectrix.h                | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 platformio.ini                   |  1 -
 src/services/firmware_update.cpp | 24 ++++++++++++++++-----
 src/zectrix.cpp                  | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/zectrix.md b/docs/zectrix.md
index b1d9dad..a6fd54c 100644
--- a/docs/zectrix.md
+++ b/docs/zectrix.md
@@ -101,8 +101,10 @@ trying another driver.
 
 ## Deliberate limitations
 
-- Upstream TRMNL OTA is disabled for these targets. An official OG/X image
-  could use incompatible pins and power behavior.
+- OTA accepts only an image built for the same Zectrix target. Such an image
+  contains the string `TRMNL-ZECTRIX-IMAGE:<model>`. An official OG/X image
+  uses other pins and power behavior, so the update is refused before it is
+  made bootable.
 - Factory QA is disabled because its fixtures and pin assumptions are for
   official TRMNL hardware.
 - Only the Home / OK button is mapped into the current single-button TRMNL
diff --git a/include/zectrix.h b/include/zectrix.h
index 3d55021..1b2ae24 100644
--- a/include/zectrix.h
+++ b/include/zectrix.h
@@ -10,6 +10,37 @@ void zectrix_power_init();
 // deep sleep.
 void zectrix_prepare_deep_sleep();
 
+#include <Arduino.h>
+#include <config.h>
+
+// OTA image check. Every image built for this board contains
+// ZECTRIX_IMAGE_ID. ZectrixImageCheck passes an OTA stream through to
+// Update and tells if the image contained the ID, so an official TRMNL image
+// (other pins and power behavior) is never made bootable.
+#define ZECTRIX_IMAGE_ID "TRMNL-ZECTRIX-IMAGE:" DEVICE_MODEL
+
+class ZectrixImageCheck : public Stream {
+public:
+  explicit ZectrixImageCheck(Stream &source);
+
+  bool found() const { return _matched == _length; }
+
+  int available() override { return _source.available(); }
+  int peek() override { return _source.peek(); }
+  int read() override;
+  using Stream::readBytes;
+  size_t readBytes(char *buffer, size_t length) override;
+  size_t write(uint8_t) override { return 0; }
+
+private:
+  void scan(const uint8_t *data, size_t length);
+
+  Stream &_source;
+  size_t _length;
+  size_t _matched = 0;
+  uint8_t _fallback[64];
+};
+
 // Charger status lines. Valid after zectrix_power_init().
 bool zectrix_is_charging();
 bool zectrix_is_charged();
